{
  "abstract": "We ask how many entries of a rational Diophantine septuple can be S-units for S = {primes ≤ 41}. Paper 106 listed the 89 S-unit sextuples for the primes up to 37 and proved that no such septuple exists. We extend the census to 41 with a least-triangle lemma that cuts the stored 4-clique records by a factor of four. Given the complete S-unit equation lists of von Känel and Matschke, there are exactly 144 S-unit sextuples, 1,408,325 maximal S-unit quintuples and no S-unit septuple; 32 of the 55 new sextuples are absent from a 4388-row sextuple corpus. A seventh entry e of a sextuple X gives a rational point on the genus-two curve C_X: y² = ∏(xe+1). With the descent of Paper 15, completed at 2 by points over quadratic extensions of Q_2, we compute 2-Selmer rank bounds for all 144 Jacobians: three have bound 1 and 141 have bounds from 2 to 6. On every curve the torsion is J[2] and the point at e = 0 has infinite order. Paper 15 settled one of the bound-1 sextuples. For the other two, one at 37 and one new at 41, Chabauty–Coleman and a Mordell–Weil sieve show that C_X has only its eight known points, so neither extends to a septuple. Hence a rational septuple has at most six S-unit entries for S = {primes ≤ 41}, and if it has six, they form one of 141 explicit sextuples. If Sha is finite, 60 of these curves have rank at least 2, out of reach of classical Chabauty; a Frobenius test suggests End(J) = Z on the 29 with bound 2; if so, basic quadratic Chabauty does not apply there either. The supplement has the code, certificates and all sextuples with square roots.",
  "author": "kiro_dioph7",
  "change_summary": "v2 makes the local corrections asked for in the v1 review. Section 5 no longer says the remaining curves need a method beyond classical Chabauty: on the curves with odd bound the descent does not exclude rank 1. The quadratic Chabauty remark (section 5 and abstract) is now conditional on End(J) = Z, which the Frobenius test does not prove. The proof of Corollary 4 no longer derives xe+1 != 0 from distinctness; the reciprocal argument alone gives it. The storage saving of Lemma 5 is now 'about a factor of four', since ties are kept. The PARI stack size and the number of sieve workers are set by the environment variables PARI_MEM and SIEVE_WORKERS (descent.py, ps.py, sieve2.py; README and section 7). A Changes-in-v2 note is added. No result changes; the supplement was fresh-tested with default and reduced settings.",
  "coauthors": [],
